Meta.DisplayName=Bannerlord TAOM (AMP3)
Meta.Description=Mount & Blade II: Bannerlord with the TAOM overhaul (Tales from the Age of Men) on a Coop dedicated server under Wine. Same engine as the Bannerlord Coop (modpacks) template, but its own application id, its own ports and its own modpack default, so TAOM work can never move the vanilla template. The module list is built from modpacks/taom.json, not hardcoded: The module list the dedicated server needs is passed as an argument (_MODULES_*A*B*_MODULES_) and built from an ordered manifest instead of being hardcoded, so a modpack is a data file: add, remove or reorder modules without touching the template. Module archives come from their official source and their size and sha256 are checked before extraction; a missing or mismatched module fails the start with an explicit list rather than serving a half-loaded world. The vanilla pack reproduces the module order of the CDN template and acts as a witness.
Meta.OS=Linux
Meta.AarchSupport=Unknown
Meta.Arch=x86_64
Meta.Author=Hellm4n
Meta.URL=https://github.com/Hellm4nbot/amp-templates/blob/main/README.md#bannerlord-taom
Meta.DisplayImageSource=steam:261550
Meta.EndpointURIFormat=
Meta.ConfigManifest=bannerlord-taomconfig.json
Meta.MetaConfigManifest=bannerlord-taommetaconfig.json
Meta.ConfigRoot=bannerlord-taom.kvp
Meta.MinAMPVersion=2.4.0.6
Meta.SpecificDockerImage=cubecoders/amp3base:wine-stable
Meta.DockerRequired=False
Meta.ContainerPolicy=RecommendedOnLinux
Meta.ContainerPolicyReason=The server requires Wine (ideally latest stable from winehq.org) to run on Linux, as BannerlordCoopServer.exe has no native Linux build. Using a container avoids the need to install Wine on the host.
Meta.ExtraSetupStepsURI=
